# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# Static site (no logins, cookies, or sensitive data), so the security surface
# is small — we set the two genuinely worthwhile, zero-risk headers (HSTS to
# pin HTTPS, X-Frame-Options to block clickjacking via framing) and make the
# two Cloudflare already sends explicit. No CSP: it adds maintenance + breakage
# risk (Carto tiles, unpkg, SheetJS, GA, TfL API) for little gain on a static
# read-only map.
#
# Scripts and styles must revalidate on every load, like the HTML and the
# /data JSONs already do. Without an explicit rule, Pages' default gave them
# max-age=14400 — so for up to 4 h after a deploy, returning browsers ran the
# previous JS/CSS against the new HTML and silently missed features (observed
# 2026-07-31). There are no fingerprinted filenames in this no-build setup, so
# revalidation is the only safe policy; with ETags each check is a 304 and the
# module graph loads consistently versioned. Rule blocks below stay
# comment-free — the _headers parser only reliably tolerates comments up here.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
